================================================================================
SCOPE AND A NOTE ON THE CURRICULUM TEXT
================================================================================

The MIT license above covers the SOFTWARE in this repository: the build scripts,
the audit and verification guards, the React site under `learning-site/`, the
CI workflows, and the configuration.

The CURRICULUM TEXT -- the Markdown under `ai-roadmaps/`, the research notes
under `docs/research/`, and the explanatory prose in `HANDOVER.md` -- is
additionally offered under the terms of the Creative Commons Attribution 4.0
International License (CC BY 4.0):

    https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/

You are free to share and adapt that material for any purpose, including
commercially, provided you give appropriate credit, link to the license, and
indicate whether changes were made.

WHY THE SPLIT: code and prose have different needs. The tooling is more useful to
others under a permissive software license with no attribution friction. The
written curriculum is more useful if people can reuse and adapt it for their own
teaching, which is what CC BY 4.0 permits, while the attribution requirement
keeps a record of where the material came from.

